// A list of list literals whose later inner literal has the wider leaf is built at that leaf,
// which the checker joined the element to (D4876). The proof divides an element of the first,
// narrower inner literal, so one left in the i32 rep cannot print the answer.
//
// Format: scripts/capability-probes/README.md, "Template format".
// @@VALUE@@
[[1, 2], [3.5]]
// @@TYPE@@
f64[][]
// @@PROOF@@
print(v[0][1] / 4.0 + v[1][0])
// @@WANT@@
4
// @@VALUE2@@
[[[1]], [[2.5]]]
// @@TYPE2@@
f64[][][]
// @@PROOF2@@
print(v[0][0][0] / 4.0 + v[1][0][0])
// @@WANT2@@
2.75
// @@SKIP@@
is_in_if: the value is a list, not a union — there is no arm to test it against
is_in_while: same
is_in_and: same
is_in_not: same
else_if: same
early_return_guard: same
